\f0\fs24 \cf0 tools:\
* nImOaddChannel 'a' ['b'] - add a channel to the node 'a' with 'b' = true adding an output and 'b' = false adding an input ('b' defaults to false); 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
\cf2 * nImObridge 'a' 'b' \'97 routing between networks; 'a' is the name of this network, 'b' is the address to connect to the other\
\cf0 * nImOcheck - returns zero if the registry detected and non-zero otherwise, so that scripts can start the registry; 
\f1\b DONE\

\f0\b0 * nImOclean 'a' - remove Registry information for a node or a machine; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOconnect 'c' 'd' ['m'] \'97 connects channel 'c' to channel 'd' with transport 'm' (TCP or UDP [or UDT]) [only one connection allowed between 'c' and 'd']; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOdisconnect 'c' \'97 removes connection from or to channel 'c'; 
\f1\b DONE\

\f0\b0 * nImOlist xyz \'97 reports all the known nodes, channels, connections, bridges, machines, applications depending on filters and options; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOlog - displays the log in a terminal; 
\f1\b DONE\

\f0\b0 * nImOplayback 'a' ['b' ['c']] - sends messages from a file at a specified rate; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOpost 'a' 'b' - writes text to the log; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOread \'97 writes out the string representation of messages received; 
\f1\b DONE\

\f0\b0 * nImOrecord 'a' - writes out received messages to a file; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOstart ['a' ['b']] - starts a service via a launcher; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOstop 'a' - shutdown one or all nodes or machines except active log programs; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOversion \'97 reports the versions of the libraries; 
\f1\b DONE\

\f0\b0 * nImOwrite \'97 reads the string representation of a message and sends it out a channel; 
\f1\b DONE\

\f0\b0 \
interface:\
\cf2 * nImOchart ['n'] - graphs values of messages from the 'n' input SIGNAL channels ('n' defaults to 1)\
* nImOdisplay - like 
\f1\b nImOread
\f0\b0  but GUI-based\
* nImOmanage - GUI application to display and control nImO applications\
* nImOwatch - like 
\f1\b nImOlog
\f0\b0  but GUI-based\
\cf0 \
examples:\
\cf2 * nImOricochet 'p' - forwards a message to the next machine in a list\
* nImOricochetControl 'r' 'p' - creates a machine list and sends it to one of the machines ('r' indicates whether random or sequential machine order)\
\cf0 \
signal services:\
\cf2 * nImOgate ['t'] - passes messages through when a control SIGNAL channel exceeds a specific value 't' ('t' defaults to 0)\
\cf0 * nImOnegate - changes the sign of an input SIGNAL message before sending to the output channel; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
\cf3 * nImOpower ['p'] - raises the value of an input SIGNAL message to a specific power 'p' and sends to the output channel ('p' defaults to 1)\cf0 ; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \cf3 \
* nImOproduct ['n'] - gathers values from all 'n' input SIGNAL channels and outputs the product of all the values ('n' defaults to 2)\cf0 ; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \cf3 \
\cf0 * nImOpulse ['p' ['r' ['l' ['h']]]] - sends a series of SIGNAL messages with an period of 'p' seconds and a minimum of 'l' and a maximum of 'h' with a random level if 'r' is true ('p' defaults to 1, 'r' defaults to false, 'l' defaults to 0 and 'h' defaults to 1); 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
\cf3 * nImOsum ['n'] - gathers values from all 'n' input SIGNAL channels and outputs the sum of all the values ('n' defaults to 2)\cf0 ; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \cf3 \
\cf0 \
wiring services:\
* nImOcommutator ['n' ['r']] - forwards a message to one of 'n' output channels (default 1), sequentially if 'r' is missing or false, randomly if true [default false]; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOdelay ['d'] - forwards any message from the input channel to the output channel after a delay of 'd' seconds ('d' defaults to 1); 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOfanIn ['n'] - forwards any messages from one of the 'n' input channels to the output channel ('n' defaults to 1); 
\f1\b DONE\

\f0\b0 * nImOfanOut ['n'] - forwards any messages from the input channel to all of the 'n' output channels ('n' defaults to 1); 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOjunction ['n' ['m']] - forwards any messages from one of the 'n' input channels to all of the 'm' output channels ('n' and 'm' default to 1); 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
* nImOrepeat ['d' ['e']] - forwards 'd' copies of any message from the input channel to the output channel after a delay of 'e' seconds ('d' and 'e' default to 1)
\f1\b ; DONE
\f0\b0 \
\
application support:\
\cf2 * nImOaddApp 'a' - adds an application to the list of available applications on the machine\
\cf0 * nImOlauncher 'a' - records the machine and known applications with the Registry and waits for requests to start applications; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
\cf2 * nImOloadApps 'a' - loads a set of applications\
\cf0 * nImOregistry - the Registry, one per LAN; 
\f1\b DONE
\f0\b0 \
\cf2 * nImOremoveApp 'a' - removes an application from the list of available applications on the machine\
* nImOstoreApps 'a' - stores the current set of loaded applications\
* nImOupdateApp 'a' - update an application\
\cf0 \
setup support:\
\cf2 * nImOloadSetup 'a' - loads a setup\
* nImOstoreSetup 'a' - stores a setup\
\cf0 \
programmable services:\
\cf2 * nImOjavaScript 'a' ['b' \'85 ] - loads and runs a JavaScript service\
* nImOlisp 'a' ['b' \'85 ] - loads and runs a Common Lisp service\
* nImOpython 'a' ['b' \'85 ] - loads and runs a Python service\
\cf0 \
shell script:\
* nimo\
	provides a 'simplified' command-line interface to some of the executables, using the default options \
		nimo adda <a> - invokes nImOaddApp <a>\
		nImO addc <a> <b> - invokes nImOaddChannel <a> <b>\
		nimo bridge <a> <b> - invokes nImObridge <a> <b>\
		nimo check - invokes nImOcheck\
		nimo clean <a> - invokes nImOclean <a>\
		nimo connect <c> <d> <m> - invokes nImOconnect <c> <d> <m>\
		nimo disconnect <c> - invokes nImOdisconnect <c>\
		nimo help - lists choices\
		nimo list <type> - invokes nImOlist <type>; with no <type>, lists choices\
		nimo loada <a> - invokes nImOloadApps <a>\
		nimo loads <a> - invokes nImOloadSetup <a>\
		nimo log - invokes nImOlog\
		nimo playback <a> <b> <c> - invokes nImOplayback <a> <b> <c>\
		nimo post <a> <b> - invokes nImOport <a> <b>\
		nimo read - invokes nImOread\
		nimo record <a> - invokes nImOrecord <a>\
		nimo remove <a> - invokes nImOremoveApp <a>\
		nimo start <a> <b> - invokes nImOstart <a> <b>\
		nimo stop <a> - invokes nImOstop <a>\
		nimo storea <a> - invokes nImOstoreApps <a>\
		nimo stores <a> - invokes nImOstoreSetup <a>\
		nimo update <a> - invokes nImOupdateApp <a>\
		nimo version - invokes nImOversion\
		nimo write - invokes nImOwrite\
\
